  </button>

  <!-- Pipeline -->
  <div class="pipeline" id="pipeline">
    <h3>Sealing Pipeline</h3>
    <div class="step" id="step1"><div class="status pending">&#9675;</div><div class="label"><strong>GPS + Device</strong> — Capturing location &amp; device fingerprint</div><div class="detail" id="detail1"></div></div>
    <div class="step" id="step2"><div class="status pending">&#9675;</div><div class="label"><strong>SHA-256</strong> — Computing hash for OpenTimestamps</div><div class="detail" id="detail2"></div></div>
    <div class="step" id="stepFraud"><div class="status pending">&#9675;</div><div class="label"><strong>Forensic Scan</strong> — Detecting contradictions in the document</div><div class="detail" id="detailFraud"></div></div>
    <div class="step" id="step3"><div class="status pending">&#9675;</div><div class="label"><strong>OpenTimestamps</strong> — Submitting to calendar servers</div><div class="detail" id="detail3"></div></div>
    <div class="step" id="step4"><div class="status pending">&#9675;</div><div class="label"><strong>A4 Watermark</strong> — Full-page background at 20% opacity</div><div class="detail" id="detail4"></div></div>
    <div class="step" id="step5"><div class="status pending">&#9675;</div><div class="label"><strong>Clean QR Code</strong> — Encoding hash + seal metadata (identity stays private)</div><div class="detail" id="detail5"></div></div>
    <div class="step" id="step6"><div class="status pending">&#9675;</div><div class="label"><strong>Seal Footer</strong> — Hash + timestamp on every page</div><div class="detail" id="detail6"></div></div>
    <div class="step" id="step7"><div class="status pending">&#9675;</div><div class="label"><strong>Finalize</strong> — Preparing sealed PDF package</div><div class="detail" id="detail7"></div></div>
    <div class="step" id="step8"><div class="status pending">&#9675;</div><div class="label"><strong>SHA-512</strong> — Verum Forensic Fingerprint (final verification)</div><div class="detail" id="detail8"></div></div>
  </div>

  <!-- Payment gate (commercial detection). Rendered in its OWN container so the
       static #results skeleton below (qrPreview canvas, hash displays, download
       grid) is never destroyed before the sealing pipeline needs it. -->
  <div class="results" id="paymentGate"></div>

  <!-- Results -->
  <div class="results" id="results">
    <h3>Document Sealed</h3>
    <div class="ots-status pending" id="otsStatus">&#8987; OpenTimestamps proof pending Bitcoin blockchain confirmation (typically 1-2 hours)</div>
    <div class="ots-status pending" style="display:block;line-height:1.6;border-color:rgba(212,168,67,0.4)">&#128241; This report comes from the website's deterministic engine &mdash; free for everyone, no download needed. For the <strong>full experience</strong> &mdash; the hybrid on-device AI with richer narrative reports, an evidence vault, and the legal chat &mdash; <a href="/index.html#coming-soon" style="color:var(--gold, #d4a843)">get the app that suits you</a> when they release: Android, Windows&nbsp;Lite, or the Fraud Firewall for institutions.</div>
    <div class="ots-status pending" id="asIsNote" style="display:none;">&#128274; This document is password-protected, so it was sealed exactly as-is: the SHA-512 fingerprint and blockchain timestamp cover these exact bytes and verify normally. The watermark, QR and footer could not be stamped inside the locked file &mdash; your Seal Certificate carries the seal record instead.</div>
    <div class="preview-section">
      <h4>What Your Sealed Document Looks Like</h4>
      <p>Every page has the <strong>A4 watermark</strong> as a background layer at 20% opacity. Your <strong>original document text is preserved exactly</strong> — no content is moved, scaled, or altered. The <strong>QR code</strong> sits in the top-right margin and the <strong>seal footer</strong> with your SHA-512 fingerprint appears at the bottom of every page.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="qr-section">
      <canvas id="qrPreview" width="220" height="220" style="background:white; padding:16px; border-radius:12px;"></canvas>
      <p id="qrPreviewNote">Clean QR — no border, no interfering box. Scans instantly.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hash-row"><label>SHA-256 (OpenTimestamps)</label><div class="hash-display" id="sha256Display"></div></div>
    <div class="hash-row"><label>SHA-512 (Verum Fingerprint)</label><div class="hash-display" id="sha512Display"></div></div>
    <div class="hash-row"><label>Seal ID</label><div class="hash-display" id="sealIdDisplay" style="color:#D4A843;"></div></div>
    <div class="hash-row" id="sealedHashRow" style="display:none;"><label>Sealed File SHA-512 (VO-SEAL2 self-integrity)</label><div class="hash-display" id="sealedHashDisplay" style="font-size:11px;"></div></div>
    <div class="hash-row" id="sizeRow" style="display:none;"><label>File size</label><div class="hash-display" id="sizeDisplay" style="font-size:12px;"></div></div>
    <div class="hash-row" id="chainRow" style="display:none;"><label>Chain of Custody</label><div class="hash-display" id="chainDisplay" style="color:#4A7EC7;font-size:12px;"></div></div>
    <a href="/verify.html" class="verify-link" id="verifyLink">&#128269; Verify on verumglobal.foundation</a>
    <div class="download-grid" id="downloadGrid">
      <a href="#" class="download-btn primary" id="downloadSealedPdf" download>&#11015; Download Sealed PDF</a>
      <a href="#" class="download-btn" id="downloadOts" download>&#11015; Download blockchain receipt (.ots) — PENDING</a>
      <a href="#" class="download-btn" id="downloadAnchorCert" download style="display:none;">&#11015; Download Anchor Certificate (PDF)</a>
    </div>
    <div id="otsReceiptNote" style="display:none;font-size:12px;color:#8ea3b5;margin-top:10px;line-height:1.6;">Pending: the Bitcoin anchor typically confirms within 1–2 hours. Verify this document later on verumglobal.foundation/verify.html to upgrade this receipt to a confirmed proof.</div>
  </div>

  <!-- Info Section -->
  <div class="info-section">
    <h3>How Document Sealing Works</h3>
    <p>Every document sealed by Verum Omnis receives a forensic-grade cryptographic seal that makes it tamper-evident and court-admissible.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="item"><h4>&#128220; A4 Watermark Background</h4><p>The full-page Verum Omnis watermark is applied at 20% opacity behind your content. Your original document text is preserved exactly — the QR code sits in the natural page margin.</p></div>
      <div class="item"><h4>&#128241; Clean QR Code</h4><p>QR sits in the top-right margin with white background panel — never covers document text. Original document layout is fully preserved. Scans instantly with any phone.</p></div>
      <div class="item"><h4>&#128274; Dual Hash</h4><p>SHA-256 for OpenTimestamps blockchain anchoring. SHA-512 as the Verum forensic fingerprint. Two independent hashes, zero trust required.</p></div>
      <div class="item"><h4>&#9939; Bitcoin Blockchain</h4><p>OpenTimestamps anchors the SHA-256 hash into Bitcoin. Once confirmed (~1-2 hours), the timestamp is permanently and independently verifiable.</p></div>
      <div class="item"><h4>&#128100; Identity Pipeline</h4><p>Optional sender identity (name, ID, address, email) is written into your private Seal Certificate for affidavit pre-fill and chain of custody — never into the public QR code unless you explicitly opt in.</p></div>
      <div class="item"><h4>&#128205; GPS + Device</h4><p>Automatic geolocation and device fingerprint capture. Proves where and from what device the seal was applied.</p></div>
      <div class="item"><h4>&#128272; Password Protection</h4><p>Optional AES-256 password protection with delivery receipt cover page. Recipient must email sender for password — that email IS the read receipt.</p></div>
      <div class="item"><h4>&#128737; Tamper Detection</h4><p>Recipient uploads document to verify page. If SHA-512 doesn't match --> "TAMPERED — DO NOT ACCEPT". Cryptographically impossible to forge.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="site-footer">
    Verum Omnis Foundation — Patent Pending<br>
    Constitution v6.0 Final — Article X Non-Weaponization Doctrine
  </div>

